---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "@/config/site";

const updated = "August 2, 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="Review the rules, limitations and responsibilities that apply when using Toolsiva."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 lg:py-16">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-brand-300">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-white sm:text-4xl">Terms of Use</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-zinc-500">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <div class="prose-premium mt-10 space-y-10 text-sm leading-7 text-zinc-300">
      <section><h2>1. Agreement to these terms</h2><p>By accessing or using Toolsiva, you agree to these Terms of Use and the Privacy Policy. If you do not agree, do not use the service.</p></section>
      <section><h2>2. Description of the service</h2><p>Toolsiva provides browser-based utilities for text transformation, developer data, security-related tasks, QR generation, calculations and unit conversions. Features may be added, changed or removed over time.</p></section>
      <section><h2>3. Eligibility and lawful use</h2><p>You may use Toolsiva only when you are legally able to accept these terms and only for lawful purposes. You are responsible for complying with laws, contracts, workplace rules and third-party rights that apply to your use.</p></section>
      <section><h2>4. Your input and output</h2><p>You retain responsibility for information you enter and results you create. Do not submit content you are not authorized to process. You are responsible for reviewing generated output before copying, publishing, transmitting or relying on it.</p></section>
      <section><h2>5. Prohibited conduct</h2><p>You must not interfere with the service, bypass security controls, distribute malware, attempt unauthorized access, overload infrastructure, scrape at an abusive rate, misrepresent affiliation with Toolsiva or use the service to violate another person's rights.</p></section>
      <section><h2>6. Accuracy and verification</h2><p>Tool results may be affected by incorrect input, rounding, browser behavior, implementation defects, changing standards or limitations described on a page. Important results should be independently verified using an authoritative source.</p></section>
      <section><h2>7. No professional advice</h2><p>Toolsiva does not provide legal, financial, tax, medical, engineering, cybersecurity or other professional advice. Tools involving health, money, safety or legal consequences are general informational aids only.</p></section>
      <section><h2>8. Security-related tools</h2><p>Password, token, hash, encoding and decoding tools do not make a wider system secure. Security also depends on storage, transmission, access control, implementation, configuration and current standards.</p></section>
      <section><h2>9. Intellectual property</h2><p>The Toolsiva name, visual identity, original interface, text and software are protected by applicable intellectual-property laws. These terms permit use of the service but do not transfer ownership of Toolsiva materials.</p></section>
      <section><h2>10. Third-party services and links</h2><p>Toolsiva may use or link to third-party services. Their availability, content, security and privacy practices are controlled by their respective operators. A link does not imply endorsement.</p></section>
      <section><h2>11. Availability and modification</h2><p>The service is provided without a guarantee of uninterrupted availability. Toolsiva may update, suspend, limit or discontinue any feature to maintain security, quality, compliance or operational sustainability.</p></section>
      <section><h2>12. Disclaimer of warranties</h2><p>To the extent permitted by law, Toolsiva is provided “as is” and “as available” without warranties of accuracy, reliability, fitness for a particular purpose, merchantability, non-infringement or continuous operation.</p></section>
      <section><h2>13. Limitation of liability</h2><p>To the maximum extent permitted by law, Toolsiva and its operators will not be liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, exemplary or punitive damages, loss of data, loss of profits or decisions made from tool results.</p></section>
      <section><h2>14. Indemnity</h2><p>Where permitted by law, you agree to be responsible for claims and costs arising from your unlawful misuse of the service, violation of these terms or infringement of third-party rights.</p></section>
      <section><h2>15. Changes to these terms</h2><p>These terms may be revised as the service evolves. Continued use after an updated version becomes effective indicates acceptance of the revised terms.</p></section>
      <section>
        <h2>16. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these terms may be sent to{" "}
          <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`}>{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
